<title>CANADA: Bombardier unit in Belgian subway deal.</title>
<headline>Bombardier unit in Belgian subway deal.</headline>
<dateline>SAINT BRUNO, Quebec 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bombardier Inc said on Thursday the Belgian division of Bombardier Eurorail was awarded half of an estimated C$80 million contract to build 25 subway cars for Brussels' transit authority.</p>
<p>Bombardier's Belgian unit was executing the contract with GEC Alsthom ACEC Transport, a unit of GEC-Alsthom NV, Bombardier said.</p>
<p>&quot;The order is valued at approximately C$80 million, of which Bombardier's share is approximately C$40 million,&quot; Bombardier said.  </p>
<p>The subway cars for the Societe des Transports Intercommunaux de Bruxelles would be built at Eurorail's facilities in Manage and Bruges, Belgium.</p>
<p>Deliveries would be made between May and December 1999, Bombardier said.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
</text>
